BandC wrote:
> I'm sure this has been asked before but I haven't seen anything lately
> so I'll ask. How do people in this newsgroup feel about Slash 'em?

In short:  It's different.  I'll stick (mainly) to vanilla.

I've tried some slash'em games - mainly as "in between" games while I
was trying to ascend my extinctionist Tourist.

The first thing you notice about it is that it is different.  I'd
recommend it out for players who get bored with how similar
every game they play becomes (especially once you hit gehenom)
as there are a number of surprises that keep you on your toes.
There are also a lot more options to explore, (artifacts, asection
kit makeup, firearm, doppelgangers/vampire/lycanthrope
characters) which IMHO makes the game more interesting
(for a while at least).

I also feel that it's harder to compare ascentions.  In Vanilla, every
ascention is bragworthy.  In slashem, I think that ascending
(for example) a Lawful Valk is easier than in vanilla (#twoweapon
Excalibur and Mojo, and identify everything in shops) while getting
anywhere with a lycanthrope/vampire character means dealing with
a bunch of serious starting problems.

I also tried the Lethe Patch to slashem.  If you think "vanilla"
slashem is bad....  (Lethe has around 70 dungeon levels) The
game crashed somewhere in the middle of gehenom (trying to
move my pets downstairs), so I don't think I'll go back there soon,
(though I would like to meet Cthulhu).

Anyway.

It's fun, and there are some things I'd like to see imported into
vanilla, but I think I'll stick with the regular game.

